Tools and Methodology 

For data cleanning, I used Excel ( Power query for data cleaning and Power pivot to calculate new measures)

-Irrelevant fields such as the zip code column were removed to streamline the dataset. Text standardization was applied by 
transforming the city field to ensure consistent capitalization.
-A new calculated column was created to determine customer age by deriving the duration from the birthdate, converting it into years,
and rounding it to the nearest whole number. Building on this, a conditional column was introduced to segment customers into age 
groups (Young Adult, Adult, Senior) based on defined business logic, enabling more meaningful demographic analysis.
-To support time-based analysis, a dedicated calendar table was created containing a continuous range of dates aligned with the 
sales data. 
-Additional date-related attributes, including day name, start of week, start of month, start of quarter, and year, were generated 
to enhance data slicing and support multidimensional analysis within Power Pivot. This structured approach ensured that the dataset 
was clean, consistent, and optimized for accurate reporting and insightful analysis.
-No relevant duplicates and missing values found .
-Data types for each variables were checked.
